IMPORT prelude

-- Scheut Missions Ordinance 1938 (Singapore) -- who the Corporation "the Procureur in the Straits Settlements of the Scheut
-- Missions" is and how a successor Procureur becomes "duly qualified" (ss 2, 5), what it may do with property and its capacity to
-- sue and be sued (s 3), the eight scheduled parcels vested in it (s 4 and the two Schedules), how its deeds are validly sealed and
-- signed (s 6), and whose rights the Ordinance leaves alone (s 7).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/SMO1938.txt. The deposit says the edition
-- "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021". One amendment
-- annotation appears in the body: "[7/97]" under s 7. The Ordinance is dated 16 September 1938. The deposit's metadata records it
-- as the current version as at 1 October 2026. The arrangement of sections at the top of the deposit is printed out of step with
-- the numbers; the body's numbering (ss 1-7) is followed here.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0249 in ../../../requirements.jsonl: tier 4 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by everyday-life
-- relevance. It asks what the Ordinance decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a sharper question
-- yet. The operative part is seven short sections, so the whole of it is in scope except the short title. For a person outside the
-- Mission it matters when buying, leasing or lending against the Corporation's land (ss 3, 6), when suing it (s 3), and for title
-- to the eight parcels in the Schedules (ss 4, 7).
--
-- NOT ENCODED: s 1 (short title); s 2(2) (the seal may be broken and made anew); the recitals, except as they explain the
-- Schedules; the content of s 48 of the Conveyancing and Law of Property Act 1886, to which ss 5(1) and 6(1) refer (whether an
-- instrument was filed or a power deposited under it is a stated fact); the boundaries and grant histories of each parcel; whether
-- any parcel is still held (the deposit does not say); the Mission's internal governance.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Scheut Missions Ordinance 1938 -- the Corporation`

§§ `2 and 5 -- who is the Corporation, and when a successor Procureur is duly qualified`

-- s 2(1): "The Reverend Richard Quintens and his successors for the time being in the office of Procureur of the Missions Scheut
-- duly qualified as hereinafter provided shall be a body corporate, hereinafter called the Corporation", with perpetual succession
-- and a corporate seal.
-- s 5(1): "No person other than the said Richard Quintens shall be deemed to be duly qualified as aforesaid unless and until he has
-- first, with the approval of the Minister signified under his hand and seal, caused the power of attorney or other instrument
-- constituting him Procureur to be duly filed in the Registry of the Supreme Court at Singapore pursuant to section 48 of the
-- Conveyancing and Law of Property Act 1886 and unless and until a notification of such filing has appeared in the Gazette."
-- s 5(2): "Such notification shall be sufficient evidence of the appointment and that the person therein named is duly qualified".
--
-- Four things, all required: an instrument constituting him Procureur, the Minister's approval "under his hand and seal", filing in
-- the Supreme Court Registry, and a Gazette notification of the filing. Quintens, named in 1938, needed none of them. The
-- notification is "sufficient", not "conclusive", evidence.
DECLARE Procureur HAS
    `is Richard Quintens` IS A BOOLEAN
    `holds a power of attorney or instrument constituting him Procureur` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Minister approved under his hand and seal` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the instrument was filed in the Supreme Court Registry` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the filing was notified in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the procureur` IS A Procureur
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is duly qualified` IF
        `the procureur`'s `is Richard Quintens`
    OR  (    `the procureur`'s `holds a power of attorney or instrument constituting him Procureur`
         AND `the procureur`'s `the Minister approved under his hand and seal`
         AND `the procureur`'s `the instrument was filed in the Supreme Court Registry`
         AND `the procureur`'s `the filing was notified in the Gazette`)

GIVEN `the procureur` IS A Procureur
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Gazette is sufficient evidence of qualification` IF
    `the procureur`'s `the filing was notified in the Gazette`

§§ `3 -- what the Ordinance empowers the Corporation to do`

-- s 3: "The Corporation may acquire, purchase, take, hold and enjoy movable and immovable property of every description and may
-- sell, convey and assign, surrender and yield up, mortgage, demise, re-assign, transfer or otherwise dispose of any movable or
-- immovable property vested in the Corporation upon such terms as to the Corporation seem fit and may sue and be sued by such name
-- of the Procureur in the Straits Settlements of the Scheut Missions in all Courts of Justice."
--
-- Acquiring carries no territorial limit (the Portuguese Missions Ordinance 1910 s 4 says "within the Colony"; this one does not).
-- Disposing is limited to property "vested in the Corporation". Suing and being sued is "in all Courts of Justice", not confined to
-- property. The Ordinance confers no power to borrow without security and says nothing about service of process.
DECLARE Power IS ONE OF
    `acquire or purchase property`
    `hold and enjoy property`
    `sell or convey property`
    `mortgage property`
    `lease property`
    `sue or be sued in its corporate name`
    `borrow money without security`

GIVEN `the power` IS A Power, `the property is vested in the Corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Ordinance empowers the Corporation to` IF
    CONSIDER `the power`
    WHEN `acquire or purchase property` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `hold and enjoy property` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `sell or convey property` THEN `the property is vested in the Corporation`
    WHEN `mortgage property` THEN `the property is vested in the Corporation`
    WHEN `lease property` THEN `the property is vested in the Corporation`
    WHEN `sue or be sued in its corporate name` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `4 and the Schedules -- the eight parcels`

-- s 4: "Subject to section 7 the lands and premises described in the Schedules are hereby vested in the Corporation for the estate
-- and interest for which the same are held."
-- The recitals: the First Schedule lands "were purchased" in the name of Richard Quintens, the agent; the Second Schedule land was
-- purchased in the name of "the former agent", Father Michael De Meester, who "died on 22 March 1934 in Manila". Both out of "funds
-- belonging to the Mission".
-- Items are numbered 1-8 across the two Schedules. Item 3 is "3 pieces of land" (Lots 10612, 10613, 10614 of Mukim XXV) of
-- 1,617.1, 1,599.6 and 1,580.6 m2. Item 4 was "estimated to contain an area of 674.4 m2" in the 1931 mortgage plan and "is now
-- estimated according to recent Government Resurvey to contain an area of 679.7 m2"; the resurvey figure is used. Items 5, 6 and 7
-- each lost a portion "acquired by the Municipal Commissioners" (35.4, 28.0 and 118.1 m2); the area stated for each is what remains.
-- Unlike the Portuguese Missions Ordinance, no Schedule item states a lease term or a rent.
DECLARE Parcel IS ONE OF
    `item 1, Ulu Pandan, Lot 24196`
    `item 2, Ulu Pandan, Lot 24199`
    `item 3, Geylang, Lots 10612 to 10614`
    `item 4, Killiney Road, Lot 1311`
    `item 5, Claymore, Lot 242`
    `item 6, Somerset Road, Lot 252`
    `item 7, Somerset Road, Lot 232`
    `item 8, Nassim Road, Lot 55`

GIVEN `the parcel` IS A Parcel
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Schedule it is in` `the parcel` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the parcel`
    WHEN `item 8, Nassim Road, Lot 55` THEN 2
    OTHERWISE 1

-- Whose name the land was purchased in, per the recitals.
GIVEN `the parcel` IS A Parcel
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `was purchased in the name of the deceased former agent` IF
    `the Schedule it is in` `the parcel` EQUALS 2

GIVEN `the parcel` IS A Parcel
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the area in square metres` `the parcel` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the parcel`
    WHEN `item 1, Ulu Pandan, Lot 24196` THEN 1013.6
    WHEN `item 2, Ulu Pandan, Lot 24199` THEN 831.5
    WHEN `item 3, Geylang, Lots 10612 to 10614` THEN 1617.1 PLUS 1599.6 PLUS 1580.6
    WHEN `item 4, Killiney Road, Lot 1311` THEN 679.7
    WHEN `item 5, Claymore, Lot 242` THEN 435.8
    WHEN `item 6, Somerset Road, Lot 252` THEN 402.1
    WHEN `item 7, Somerset Road, Lot 232` THEN 1508.2
    WHEN `item 8, Nassim Road, Lot 55` THEN 7881.5

-- The portion each lot lost to the Municipal Commissioners of the Town of Singapore, as the Schedule states it.
GIVEN `the parcel` IS A Parcel
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the portion acquired by the Municipal Commissioners in square metres` `the parcel` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the parcel`
    WHEN `item 5, Claymore, Lot 242` THEN 35.4
    WHEN `item 6, Somerset Road, Lot 252` THEN 28.0
    WHEN `item 7, Somerset Road, Lot 232` THEN 118.1
    OTHERWISE 0

-- The number of houses the Schedule says are erected on the land: Nos. 19, 21, 23 and 25 Killiney Road (item 4); No. 90 Somerset
-- Road (item 6); No. 100 Somerset Road (item 7); No. 24 Nassim Road (item 8). Items 1, 2, 3 and 5 mention no building.
GIVEN `the parcel` IS A Parcel
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of houses named on it` `the parcel` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the parcel`
    WHEN `item 4, Killiney Road, Lot 1311` THEN 4
    WHEN `item 6, Somerset Road, Lot 252` THEN 1
    WHEN `item 7, Somerset Road, Lot 232` THEN 1
    WHEN `item 8, Nassim Road, Lot 55` THEN 1
    OTHERWISE 0

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the total area of the First Schedule` MEANS
          `the area in square metres` `item 1, Ulu Pandan, Lot 24196`
    PLUS  `the area in square metres` `item 2, Ulu Pandan, Lot 24199`
    PLUS  `the area in square metres` `item 3, Geylang, Lots 10612 to 10614`
    PLUS  `the area in square metres` `item 4, Killiney Road, Lot 1311`
    PLUS  `the area in square metres` `item 5, Claymore, Lot 242`
    PLUS  `the area in square metres` `item 6, Somerset Road, Lot 252`
    PLUS  `the area in square metres` `item 7, Somerset Road, Lot 232`

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the total area of the scheduled parcels` MEANS
    `the total area of the First Schedule` PLUS `the area in square metres` `item 8, Nassim Road, Lot 55`

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the total land taken by the Municipal Commissioners` MEANS
          `the portion acquired by the Municipal Commissioners in square metres` `item 5, Claymore, Lot 242`
    PLUS  `the portion acquired by the Municipal Commissioners in square metres` `item 6, Somerset Road, Lot 252`
    PLUS  `the portion acquired by the Municipal Commissioners in square metres` `item 7, Somerset Road, Lot 232`

-- s 4 vests only land "described in the Schedules", and only "for the estate and interest for which the same are held": it passes
-- what the nominee held, no more. Other property the Corporation holds comes to it under s 3, not s 4.
GIVEN `is described in a Schedule` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 4 vests it in the Corporation` IF
    `is described in a Schedule`

§§ `6 -- sealing and signing the Corporation's instruments`

-- s 6(1): no instrument sealed with the Corporation's seal "shall be deemed to be duly sealed unless such seal has been affixed in
-- the presence of the said Richard Quintens or his attorney duly authorised by a power of attorney deposited under section 48 of the
-- Conveyancing and Law of Property Act 1886 or in the presence of his successor for the time being in his said office of Procureur
-- and duly qualified as aforesaid and unless such deed, document or other instrument is signed by the said Richard Quintens or his
-- attorney or by his successor or the attorney of such successor as aforesaid."
-- s 6(2): "Such signing shall be taken as sufficient evidence of the due sealing of such deed, document or other instrument."
--
-- The two lists differ. The seal may be affixed before Quintens, his deposited attorney, or a qualified successor -- the presence
-- limb names no attorney of a successor. The signature may be by Quintens, his attorney, a successor, or "the attorney of such
-- successor as aforesaid". Encoded as written: a successor's attorney may sign but the seal must be affixed before the successor in
-- person. Reading "as aforesaid" in the signing limb to carry the deposit and qualification requirements is an inference.
DECLARE Officer IS ONE OF
    `Richard Quintens`
    `Quintens's attorney under a deposited power`
    `a duly qualified successor Procureur`
    `a qualified successor's attorney under a deposited power`
    `a successor Procureur not yet gazetted`
    `an attorney whose power is not deposited`
    `nobody`

DECLARE Instrument HAS
    `is sealed with the Corporation seal` IS A BOOLEAN
    `sealed in the presence of` IS AN Officer
    `signed by` IS AN Officer

GIVEN `the officer` IS AN Officer
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may witness the seal` IF
    CONSIDER `the officer`
    WHEN `Richard Quintens` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Quintens's attorney under a deposited power` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a duly qualified successor Procureur` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the officer` IS AN Officer
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may sign` IF
    CONSIDER `the officer`
    WHEN `Richard Quintens` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Quintens's attorney under a deposited power` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a duly qualified successor Procureur` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a qualified successor's attorney under a deposited power` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the instrument` IS AN Instrument
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is duly sealed under section 6` IF
        `the instrument`'s `is sealed with the Corporation seal`
    AND `may witness the seal` (`the instrument`'s `sealed in the presence of`)
    AND `may sign` (`the instrument`'s `signed by`)

GIVEN `the instrument` IS AN Instrument
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the signature is sufficient evidence of due sealing` IF
        `the instrument`'s `is sealed with the Corporation seal`
    AND `may sign` (`the instrument`'s `signed by`)

§§ `7 -- whose rights are saved`

-- s 7: "Nothing in this Ordinance shall affect the rights of the Government, or of any bodies politic or corporate, or of any other
-- persons except such as are mentioned in this Ordinance, and those claiming by, from or under them." [7/97]
--
-- Read here (an inference from the sentence, which could also be read as saving the rights of those claiming under the Government
-- and others) as: the Ordinance may affect the rights only of persons mentioned in it and those claiming by, from or under them.
-- Everyone else's rights, the Government's included, are untouched -- and s 4 vests "Subject to section 7".
GIVEN `is mentioned in the Ordinance` IS A BOOLEAN, `claims by, from or under a person mentioned` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Ordinance may affect their rights` IF
        `is mentioned in the Ordinance`
    OR  `claims by, from or under a person mentioned`
